    <span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</span>
    <h1>Hanoi Motorbike Rental: Riders With A Passenger Return Checklist</h1>
    <p>The return is the last impression of the rental and the part with the least romance and the most consequences, because it is the moment the agreement gets read against reality. For a pair, the return is double everything: two helmets, two sets of belongings, two people memories of what the machine looked like at the start. A checklist does not add work to the return; it removes the only bad kind, the kind done in a hurry at a counter with a flight in the background.</p>
    <p>This page is the return chapter of the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> cluster for riders with a passenger. The verified fleet prices are on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">cost hub</a>, general questions are on the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> page, and the three chapters that come before this one are the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/riders-with-a-passenger-bike-choice/">bike-choice page</a>, the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/riders-with-a-passenger-rental-paperwork-questions/">paperwork questions</a> and the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/riders-with-a-passenger-pickup-planning/">pickup planning page</a>.</p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p>On this page</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#sec-1">Why the return is a two-person job</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-2">The evening-before routine</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-3">Fuel, charge and the tank question</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-4">Helmets, accessories and the count-back</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-5">The condition walk-around</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-6">Timing the hand-back</a></li>
